📌 Kaise Use Karna Hai (CMD Steps)
Method 1: Root .gitignore banao
Apne project ke root folder mein jao

.gitignore naam ki file banao (Notepad ya VS Code se)

Upar wala ROOT .gitignore content paste karo

Save karo

Phir CMD mein:

cmd
git add .gitignore
cmd
git commit -m "chore: add .gitignore"
cmd
git push
Method 2: Agar kuch files pehle se track ho rahi hain (Important!)
Agar tune pehle git add . kiya tha aur venv/, node_modules/, .env, *.db jaise files already track ho gayi hain, toh sirf .gitignore banane se kaam nahi chalega. Unhe cache se hataana padega:

cmd
git rm -r --cached .
cmd
git add .
cmd
git commit -m "chore: apply .gitignore and clean tracked files"
cmd
git push
⚠️ Ye commands files ko delete nahi karti — sirf Git ke tracking se hatati hain. Local files safe rahengi.

⚠️ Super Important: .env kabhi push na karo!
Tera .env file mein Gemini API key hai. Agar wo GitHub pe chala gaya, toh:

❌ Key leak ho jayegi

❌ Koi bhi misuse kar sakta hai

❌ Google block kar dega

Isliye:

.gitignore mein .env add hai (already covered ✅)

Sirf .env.example push karo (jo dummy values ho)

backend/.env.example (ye push karna hai):
env
# Gemini API Configuration
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Database
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./data/app.db

# Upload directory
UPLOAD_DIR=./app/static/uploads

# App settings
DEBUG=True
HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=8000
frontend/.env.example:
env
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
✅ Ek Baar Check Kar Le
Push karne ke baad GitHub pe jao aur verify karo ki ye files NAHI dikh rahi:

❌ venv/ ya .venv/

❌ node_modules/

❌ .env

❌ app.db / *.sqlite

❌ __pycache__/

❌ dist/ ya build/

Agar ye sab hide ho gaye → Perfect! 🎉

🛑 Common Errors & Fix
Error	Fix
.env still visible on GitHub	git rm --cached backend/.env phir commit
venv folder push ho raha	git rm -r --cached venv/ phir commit
node_modules upload ho gaya	git rm -r --cached frontend/node_modules
.gitkeep file missing	Manually backend/app/static/uploads/.gitkeep bana
